  "fixture_topology": "Host-native RF3/three-group fixtures, one SQL worker per host. No per-node Colima/cgroup limits; not the original constrained throughput/latency comparison.",
  "implementation": [
    "After schema validation, discovery advances its cursor and omits a fresh read-authority barrier and SQL scan when the exact full-history callback is already physically retained and only native callback work is possible.",
    "Compiled alarm capability, admitted KV bindings, built-in KV service and any call/outbox/inbox work retain ordinary discovery. KV payload retirement is not represented by EffectSummary. The original post-SQL callback exclusion remains.",
    "This scheduling omission never authorizes execution or output. Callback claim, generation/attempt fencing, fresh quorum authority, exact receipt, required archive coverage, physical ownership and shutdown remain unchanged. No worker, bank, timeout or resource increase.",
    "Three fixed command prepare/submit/settle histograms expose owned phase lifetime and original errors/cancellations. Submit and settle loop bodies remain byte-identical. Preparation includes authority/writer/SQL waits; phase histograms overlap other operations and are not business request latency.",
    "Test-only failure diagnostics retain every returned producer error and observed delivery/completion snapshot before close, without changing the inner send, original assertions or request bounds. Consumer-reported completions are not durable settlement proofs."
  ],
